     1,
     "<div><font size=\"3\" face=\"Arial\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Thank you for sharing. I recoded using</span> `log_one_minus_mu1`<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> and replaced </span>&#39;dbinom&#39;<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> with </span>&#39;dbinom_robust&#39;<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">. The model ran successfully.</span></font><br></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Saturday, February 22, 2025 at 7:07:46 AM UTC-8 James Thorson wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">In case it&#39;s helpful, the implementation in tinyVAST is <a href=\"https://github.com/vast-lib/tinyVAST/blob/main/src/tinyVAST.cpp#L456-L460\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/vast-lib/tinyVAST/blob/main/src/tinyVAST.cpp%23L456-L460&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792461460405000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0OGZn7wlARuHv-Td1IShrI\">here</a>.  The term `log_one_minus_mu1`  helps with numerical overflow in calculating the Bernoulli (presence/absence) term.</div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Sat, Feb 22, 2025 at 6:36 AM Rujia Bi &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">crysta...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\"><font face=\"Arial\" size=\"3\">Dear TMB Experts,</font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal;min-height:15px\"><font face=\"Arial\" size=\"3\"><br></font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\"><font face=\"Arial\" size=\"3\">I have developed a delta model to standardize CPUE. The model runs well using a conventional delta formulation as follows:</font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal;min-height:15px\"><font face=\"Arial\" size=\"3\"><br></font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\"><font face=\"Arial\" size=\"3\" color=\"#0000ff\">Type prob = 1 / (1 + exp(-eta1)); // Encounter probability</font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\"><font face=\"Arial\" size=\"3\" color=\"#0000ff\">Type pcat= exp(eta2); // Positive catch in number</font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\"><font face=\"Arial\" size=\"3\" color=\"#0000ff\">Type mu = prob* pcat;</font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal;min-height:15px\"><font face=\"Arial\" size=\"3\"><br></font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\"><font face=\"Arial\" size=\"3\">However, when I switched to a Poisson-link model, I encountered the following error:</font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\"><font face=\"Arial\" size=\"3\">Error in iterate(par): Newton dropout because inner gradient had non-finite components.</font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\"><font face=\"Arial\" size=\"3\">Warning message:</font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\"><font face=\"Arial\" size=\"3\">In nlminb(obj$par, obj$fn, obj$gr) : NA/NaN function evaluation.</font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal;min-height:15px\"><font face=\"Arial\" size=\"3\"><br></font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\"><font face=\"Arial\" size=\"3\">In my Poisson-link formulation, I used:</font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal;min-height:15px\"><font face=\"Arial\" size=\"3\"><br></font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\"><font face=\"Arial\" size=\"3\" color=\"#0000ff\">// Poisson-link</font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\"><font face=\"Arial\" size=\"3\" color=\"#0000ff\">Type lambda = exp(eta1);</font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\"><font face=\"Arial\" size=\"3\" color=\"#0000ff\">Type log_prob = logspace_sub(Type(0.0), -lambda); </font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\"><font face=\"Arial\" size=\"3\" color=\"#0000ff\">Type prob = exp(log_prob);</font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal;min-height:15px\"><font face=\"Arial\" size=\"3\" color=\"#0000ff\">      </font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\"><font face=\"Arial\" size=\"3\" color=\"#0000ff\"> // Positive</font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\"><font face=\"Arial\" size=\"3\" color=\"#0000ff\">Type log_pcat = eta1 + eta2  - log_prob;</font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal;min-height:15px\"><font face=\"Arial\" size=\"3\" color=\"#0000ff\">      </font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\"><font face=\"Arial\" size=\"3\" color=\"#0000ff\">// Prob * positive</font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\"><font face=\"Arial\" size=\"3\" color=\"#0000ff\">Type mu = exp(eta1 + eta2);</font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal;min-height:15px\"><font face=\"Arial\" size=\"3\"><br></font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\"><font face=\"Arial\" size=\"3\">I suspect that the error might be due to numerical issues arising from the use of logspace_sub and the subsequent exponentiation, which might be causing the gradient to produce non-finite values.</font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal;min-height:15px\"><font face=\"Arial\" size=\"3\"><br></font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\"><font face=\"Arial\" size=\"3\">Could you please advise on possible modifications or improvements to stabilize the numerical calculations in this Poisson-link model? Any guidance or suggestions would be greatly appreciated.</font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal;min-height:15px\"><font face=\"Arial\" size=\"3\"><br></font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\"><font face=\"Arial\" size=\"3\">Thanks!<br></font></p>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nTo post to this group, send email to <a rel=\"nofollow\">us...@tmb-project.org</a>. Before posting, please check the wiki and issuetracker at <a href=\"https://github.com/kaskr/adcomp/\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/kaskr/adcomp/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792461460405000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2r1wHRQvUp1ea_jGrsudpe\">https://github.com/kaskr/adcomp/</a>. Please try to create a simple repeatable example to go with your question (e.g issues 154, 134, 51). Use the issuetracker to report bugs.<br>\r\n--- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;TMB Users&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a rel=\"nofollow\">tmb-users+...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/tmb-users/57390e8e-ffb0-41e3-9988-471aa2522955n%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/tmb-users/57390e8e-ffb0-41e3-9988-471aa2522955n%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792461460405000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1PcmgLujF5h0HGqE01gE_3\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/tmb-users/57390e8e-ffb0-41e3-9988-471aa2522955n%40googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\n</blockquote></div>\r\n</blockquote></div>"
